window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-83c551f7d58c2e6c"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"prepare-a-committee-packet\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"_1\">准备委员会会议资料包</h1> <p>将治理背景整理成可供会议审阅的资料包。</p> <p>借助以往会议纪要、政策草案、相关方反馈、项目数据、治理规则和决策标准，准备带来源依据的决策简报、备选方案、议程及会议纪要模板。</p> <p><a id=\"best-for\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">适合哪些情况</h2> <ul> <li>需要就具体事项作出决定的教职员工和学术委员会。</li> <li>需要审阅有来源依据的方案、权衡因素和未解决问题的会议。</li> <li>最终判断权必须留给委员会的治理流程。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"skills-plugins\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">技能与插件</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>技能或插件</th> <th>用途</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><code>google-drive</code></td> <td>收集以往会议纪要、政策草案、反馈、项目数据和治理规则。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>$documents</code></td> <td>创建决策简报、议程和会议纪要草稿模板。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><a id=\"starter-prompt\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">起步提示词</h2> <p>准备委员会决策资料包</p> <p>建议推理级别：<code>medium</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">请审阅我提供的以往会议纪要、政策草案、相关方反馈、项目数据、治理规则、决策标准和会议截止日期。\n\n请创建一份资料包，包含：\n- 需要解决的问题\n- 有来源依据的证据\n- 备选方案及其权衡\n- 未解决的问题\n- 建议的会议议程\n- 会议纪要草稿模板\n\n将调查发现与建议分开，并把最终决定留给委员会。\n</code></pre> <p><a id=\"related-links\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">关联文档</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">插件</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"frame-the-decision\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_6\">明确要作出的决定</h2> <p>先说明委员会必须解决的具体问题、适用的治理规则、决策标准和截止日期。再补充以往会议纪要、政策草案、相关方反馈和有关项目数据。</p> <p>告诉 ChatGPT 哪些材料属于权威依据，哪些只是提案或意见。</p> <p><a id=\"assemble-the-packet\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_7\">整理会议资料包</h2> <p>使用起始提示词创建资料包，并区分：</p> <ul> <li>已确认事实及其来源证据</li> <li>对材料的解读</li> <li>可行的备选方案</li> <li>权衡因素和依赖关系</li> <li>尚未解决的政策或数据问题</li> <li>需要委员会讨论的建议</li> </ul> <p>议程应按照决策顺序安排；会议纪要模板则应便于记录结果、负责人和后续事项。</p> <p><a id=\"review-before-the-meeting\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_8\">会前复核</h2> <p>检查引用、治理要求和任何保密材料。确认不同意见和不确定性都得到了公平呈现。</p> <p>委员会反馈后，可以继续让 ChatGPT 修改资料包；但最终决定和正式记录仍由委员会及指定负责人掌握。</p>","en":"<h1 id=\"prepare-a-committee-packet\">Prepare a committee packet</h1> <p>Turn governance context into a review-ready meeting packet.</p> <p>Use ChatGPT with prior minutes, policy drafts, stakeholder feedback, program data, governance rules, and decision criteria to prepare a sourced decision brief, options, agenda, and minutes template.</p> <h2 id=\"best-for\">Best for</h2> <ul> <li>Faculty and academic committees preparing for a specific decision.</li> <li>Meetings that need sourced options, tradeoffs, and unresolved questions.</li> <li>Governance workflows where the committee must retain final judgment.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"skills-plugins\">Skills &amp; Plugins</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Skill or plugin</th> <th>Why use it</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><code>google-drive</code></td> <td>Gather prior minutes, policy drafts, feedback, program data, and governance rules.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>$documents</code></td> <td>Create the decision brief, agenda, and draft minutes template.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h2 id=\"starter-prompt\">Starter prompt</h2> <p>Prepare a Committee Decision Packet</p> <p>Suggested reasoning effort：<code>medium</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Review the prior minutes, policy drafts, stakeholder feedback, program data, governance rules, decision criteria, and meeting deadline I provide.\n\nCreate a packet with:\n- the question to resolve\n- sourced evidence\n- options and tradeoffs\n- unresolved issues\n- a proposed meeting agenda\n- a draft minutes template\n\nSeparate findings from recommendations and leave the final decision to the committee.\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"related-links\">Related links</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">Plugins</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"frame-the-decision\">Frame the decision</h2> <p>Start with the exact question the committee must resolve, the governing rules, the decision criteria, and the deadline. Add prior minutes, policy drafts, stakeholder feedback, and relevant program data.</p> <p>Tell ChatGPT which materials are authoritative and which represent proposals or opinions.</p> <h2 id=\"assemble-the-packet\">Assemble the packet</h2> <p>Use the starter prompt to create a packet that separates:</p> <ul> <li>confirmed facts and source evidence</li> <li>interpretations</li> <li>viable options</li> <li>tradeoffs and dependencies</li> <li>unresolved policy or data questions</li> <li>recommendations that need committee discussion</li> </ul> <p>The agenda should follow the decision sequence, and the minutes template should make outcomes, owners, and follow-ups easy to capture.</p> <h2 id=\"review-before-the-meeting\">Review before the meeting</h2> <p>Check citations, governance requirements, and any confidential material. Confirm that dissenting views and uncertainty are represented fairly.</p> <p>Use ChatGPT to revise the packet after committee feedback, but keep the final decision and official record with the committee and designated owner.</p>"};
